// Committed signing defaults. These are the LOWEST-priority source: the
// gitignored Developer.xcconfig (when present) overrides them via #include?
// below, and any command-line -DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=... overrides both.
//
// Why per-dev: Apple bundle IDs are globally unique across developer teams, so
// a single hard-coded ID can only be signed by the team that first registered
// it. Developers on other teams override PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER (and
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM) in their local Developer.xcconfig. See Developer.xcconfig.example.

// Defaults — the team that owns the canonical bundle ID:
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = QVYZN4MJ67
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.peregrine.modelo

// Per-dev override (gitignored). Optional: absent → friend keeps the defaults.
#include? "Developer.xcconfig"
